    {
      "title": "What Triggers a Re-render",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "What Triggers a Re-render",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Render vs DOM update",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A ==render== = React calls your component to compute JSX",
                "A render can end with ==zero DOM changes==",
                "The DOM is touched only at commit"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. What triggers one",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Trigger",
                "Re-render?"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Own state setter",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Parent re-renders",
                  "{green:yes}, all children"
                ],
                [
                  "Consumed context changes",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Props change alone",
                  "{red:no}, not a trigger"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Child re-renders even with identical props",
                "Skip it by wrapping the child in ==React.memo=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake: mutating state",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "items.push(4)  // mutated in place",
                "setItems(items)  // Object.is same: skipped",
                "setItems([...items, 4])  // new array: updates"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Same reference = bail-out",
              "text": "React compares with `Object.is`. Always pass a **new** array or object."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Prop change = render?** No; parent, state, context are",
                "**Same props, child renders?** Parent render cascades",
                "**Render = DOM update?** No; the diff decides",
                "**setState(same) skipped?** `Object.is` equal"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reconciliation and the Virtual DOM",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Reconciliation and the Virtual DOM",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Virtual DOM",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Virtual DOM== = light tree of JS objects (React elements)",
                "==Reconciliation== diffs the new tree against the previous one",
                "Only the **minimal DOM changes** get committed"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Render",
                    "sub": "new tree",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Diff",
                    "sub": "vs previous",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Commit",
                    "sub": "minimal DOM changes",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Diff Rules",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Same position",
                "Result",
                "State"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Different type",
                  "Tear down, remount",
                  "{red:Lost}"
                ],
                [
                  "Same type",
                  "Update in place",
                  "{green:Kept}"
                ],
                [
                  "Key: stable id",
                  "Item matched",
                  "{green:Kept}"
                ],
                [
                  "Key: array index",
                  "Breaks on reorder, insert, remove",
                  "{red:Wrong}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Changing a `key` on purpose ==resets== that component's state"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Component defined inside a component",
              "text": "Each render makes a **new function type**, so React remounts it: state and focus are lost. Define it at module level."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why O(n), not O(n^3)?** Two heuristics: type check and keys, no full tree comparison",
                "**Type changes at same position?** Old subtree torn down, state lost",
                "**Why is `Math.random()` a bad key?** New key each render, so every item remounts",
                "**Virtual DOM faster than real DOM?** No: it is overhead that avoids needless DOM writes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "React.memo in Practice",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "React.memo in Practice",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What memo checks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==React.memo(C)== skips a render if each prop is `Object.is` equal",
                "Guards **parent-driven** renders only",
                "`areEqual` comparator: rarely needed"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Cause",
                "Memo child"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Parent renders, props equal",
                  "{green:skipped}"
                ],
                [
                  "New object, array or function prop",
                  "{red:renders}"
                ],
                [
                  "Own state change",
                  "{red:renders}"
                ],
                [
                  "Consumed context change",
                  "{red:renders}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Stable props",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inline objects, arrays, functions are **new** each render",
                "Fix with `useCallback` and `useMemo`; parent `{children}` JSX is new too"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const Row = React.memo(function Row({ item, onSelect }) {",
                "  return <li onClick={() => onSelect(item.id)}>{item.name}</li>;",
                "});",
                "const onSelect = useCallback(id => setSel(id), []);",
                "<Row item={item} onSelect={onSelect} />"
              ],
              "note": "stable onSelect lets Row skip renders"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**How are props compared?** Shallow, `Object.is` per prop",
                "**Why does an inline callback fail?** New function identity each render",
                "**Does memo block state or context renders?** No",
                "**Custom comparator?** Rarely; only for a cheap, correct check"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One bad prop",
              "text": "A single unstable prop defeats ==React.memo==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Memoization Trade-offs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Memoization Trade-offs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What They Cache",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "useMemo",
                "useCallback"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Caches",
                  "a computed ==value==",
                  "a function ==identity=="
                ],
                [
                  "Keyed by",
                  "dependency array",
                  "dependency array"
                ],
                [
                  "Costs",
                  "memory + a compare every render",
                  "same"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Worth It?",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Yes}: genuinely ==expensive== calculation",
                "{green:Yes}: feeds a ==memoized child== or an effect dependency",
                "{green:Yes}: list with many items",
                "{red:No}: cheap calculations or primitives"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Cheaper First",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Move state down== into the component that needs it",
                "==Lift static JSX up==, pass it as `children`: not re-created on state change",
                "==Measure== with the React DevTools Profiler first"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Don't wrap everything",
              "text": "Wrong or missing dependencies cause ==stale closures==. The cache is no guarantee: React may discard it."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**useMemo slower?** Cheap work: the compare costs more",
                "**useMemo vs useCallback?** Value vs function",
                "**Avoid re-renders?** Move state down, lift JSX",
                "**Slow component?** Profiler"
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Code Splitting with lazy and Suspense",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Code Splitting with lazy and Suspense",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What lazy Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Code splitting== = bundle cut into **chunks** loaded on demand",
                "Chunk boundary: dynamic `import()`",
                "`lazy` loads the module's ==default export== on first render"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const Page = lazy(() => import('./Page'));",
                "<Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>",
                "  <Page />",
                "</Suspense>"
              ],
              "note": "lazy() at module top level"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Suspense and Split Points",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lazy component needs a ==Suspense== ancestor; it shows the `fallback` while loading",
                "**Nested** boundaries: inner fallback covers only its part"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Split",
                "Verdict"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Routes",
                  "{green:first}"
                ],
                [
                  "Modal, chart, editor",
                  "{green:yes}, heavy"
                ],
                [
                  "Tiny component",
                  "{red:no}, extra request"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No Suspense above: whole root suspends, nothing new shows until the chunk loads",
                "Failed chunk rejects: wrap in an ==Error Boundary== with retry",
                "`lazy()` inside a component: remounts every render"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**What must the module export?** A `default` export of a component",
                "**No Suspense boundary?** Root suspends, no fallback, no error",
                "**Where to split?** Routes first, then heavy modals, charts, editors",
                "**Chunk fails?** Error Boundary shows a retry"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Re-render and Performance Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Re-render and Performance Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Triggers and Reconciliation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Case",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Own state, parent render, context",
                  "{blue:re-render}"
                ],
                [
                  "New reference in state",
                  "{green:update}"
                ],
                [
                  "Same reference (`Object.is`)",
                  "==bail-out=="
                ],
                [
                  "Same type",
                  "update, keep state"
                ],
                [
                  "Different type",
                  "{red:remount}, state lost"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Component defined inside a component: remounts every render",
                "Index or `Math.random()` keys break state; use stable ids"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Performance Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Profiler",
                    "sub": "measure first",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Move state down",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "React.memo",
                    "sub": "stable props",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "useMemo / useCallback",
                    "sub": "only where needed",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Split with lazy",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const Page = lazy(() => import('./Page'))",
                "<ErrorBoundary>",
                "  <Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>",
                "    <Page />",
                "  </Suspense>",
                "</ErrorBoundary>"
              ],
              "note": "call lazy() at module top level"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Error Boundary== catches chunk load failures",
                "No Suspense above it: the root suspends, nothing shows until the chunk loads"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Render vs commit?** Render calls components and diffs; commit applies the DOM changes",
                "**Stop a re-render?** `React.memo`, move state down, pass static JSX as children",
                "**Skip memoizing?** Cheap values, primitives, or no measured slowdown",
                "**Split a route bundle?** `lazy` per route, inside `Suspense`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
